#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Phase 7 (ADR D18): the robustness items TODO.md had left open once
⍝ Phase 6's fixture server (test/09) made them deterministically
⍝ reproducible — a force-kill fallback for a child that ignores stdin
⍝ being closed, opt-in stderr capture, JSON-RPC error code/data
⍝ surviving an Mcp-layer signal, and multiple concurrent child
⍝ processes in one interpreter.
⍝
⍝ Note this test deliberately starts processes that CANNOT be stopped
⍝ gracefully (test/09's `hang`, and an hour-long `sleep`) — if the
⍝ force-kill it's testing ever regresses, this script is where an
⍝ orphaned python.exe would come from, so a failure here is worth
⍝ chasing immediately rather than at leisure (TODO.md's Shell-layer
⍝ section records an orphan from an earlier run blocking a later,
⍝ unrelated dyalogscript.ps1 launch outright).
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Shell.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpc.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpcCl.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Mcp.dyalog'

fixture←'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-fixture-server.py'
toy←'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-server.py'
toycl←'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-cl-server.py'

⍝ ⍺ Check ⍵ — 0 when the condition held, 1 (after reporting) when it
⍝ didn't, so failures accumulate with nFail+←.
Check←{⍺:0 ⋄ ⎕←'FAIL: ',⍵ ⋄ 1}
nFail←0

⍝ --- 1. Force-kill: a child that ignores stdin being closed ---------
⍝ test/09's `hang` blocks forever in a wait with no timeout, so it
⍝ never notices EOF on stdin: before this phase, Stop waited out its
⍝ whole deadline and returned with the process still Running — and
⍝ still running long after the interpreter itself had gone. StopWait:1
⍝ keeps the graceful wait short so the test doesn't pay 10s for it.
h←(StopWait:1 ⋄ Timeout:2)JsonRpc.Connect fixture
:Trap 999
    {}h JsonRpc.Call'hang'
    nFail+←0 Check'expected a timeout signal from hang'
:Else
    ⎕←'hang -> timed out as expected'
:EndTrap
JsonRpc.Disconnect h
⎕←'after Stop of a hung child: Killed=',(⍕h.Shell.Killed),' Status=',h.Shell.Status
nFail+←(h.Shell.Killed≡1)Check'a hung child should have been force-killed'
nFail+←(h.Shell.Status≡'Exited')Check'a force-killed child should end up Exited'

⍝ --- 2. ...but a well-behaved child is NOT force-killed -------------
⍝ The graceful path must still be the one that runs when it can: a
⍝ server that exits on EOF should never see signal 9.
h←(StopWait:5)JsonRpc.Connect toy
r←h JsonRpc.Call('echo'(text:'graceful'))
⎕←'graceful echo -> ',r.result
JsonRpc.Disconnect h
⎕←'after Stop of a well-behaved child: Killed=',(⍕h.Shell.Killed),' Status=',h.Shell.Status
nFail+←(h.Shell.Killed≡0)Check'a child that exits on EOF must not be force-killed'
nFail+←(h.Shell.Status≡'Exited')Check'a well-behaved child should be Exited'

⍝ --- 3. Same force-kill fallback on the Content-Length transport ----
⍝ JsonRpcCl is self-contained (it talks to ⎕SHELL directly rather than
⍝ through Shell), so its Disconnect needed the same fix independently.
⍝ The CL toy server has no `hang`, but a single-threaded sleep of an
⍝ hour is indistinguishable from one for this purpose.
hcl←(StopWait:1 ⋄ Timeout:2)JsonRpcCl.Connect toycl
:Trap 999
    {}hcl JsonRpcCl.Call('sleep'(seconds:3600))
    nFail+←0 Check'expected a timeout signal from a 3600s sleep'
:Else
    ⎕←'cl sleep -> timed out as expected'
:EndTrap
JsonRpcCl.Disconnect hcl
⎕←'after CL Disconnect of a sleeping child: Killed=',(⍕hcl.Killed),' Status=',hcl.Status
nFail+←(hcl.Killed≡1)Check'a sleeping CL child should have been force-killed'
nFail+←(hcl.Status≡'Exited')Check'a force-killed CL child should end up Exited'

⍝ --- 4. Stderr capture (opt-in) -------------------------------------
⍝ Stream 2 stays discarded by default (ADR D5/D11 — a server logging
⍝ there is legal and none of our business), but is now inspectable on
⍝ request. The protocol stream must stay clean either way: the `log`
⍝ response itself has to arrive intact, not be corrupted by the stderr
⍝ line the same call produced.
h←(CaptureStderr:1)JsonRpc.Connect toy
r←h JsonRpc.Call('log'(text:'stderr line one'))
⎕←'log -> ',r.result
r←h JsonRpc.Call('log'(text:'stderr line two'))
⍝ stdout and stderr are separate streams with no ordering guarantee
⍝ between them, so give the stderr callback a moment to have run.
⎕DL 1
⎕←'captured stderr lines: ',⍕h.Shell.StderrLines
nFail+←(2=≢h.Shell.StderrLines)Check'expected exactly the two stderr lines the server logged'
nFail+←(∨/'stderr line one'∘≡¨h.Shell.StderrLines)Check'the first logged line should be captured verbatim'
nFail+←('logged'≡r.result)Check'the protocol stream must stay clean while stderr is captured'
JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⍝ Default is still discard — nothing captured, nothing leaked.
h←JsonRpc.Connect toy
{}h JsonRpc.Call('log'(text:'unwanted'))
⎕DL 1
⎕←'default CaptureStderr=',(⍕h.Shell.CaptureStderr),' lines=',⍕≢h.Shell.StderrLines
nFail+←(0=≢h.Shell.StderrLines)Check'stderr must stay discarded unless asked for'
JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⍝ Same on the CL transport.
hcl←(CaptureStderr:1)JsonRpcCl.Connect toycl
r←hcl JsonRpcCl.Call('log'(text:'cl stderr line'))
⎕DL 1
⎕←'cl captured stderr lines: ',⍕hcl.StderrLines
nFail+←(∨/'cl stderr line'∘≡¨hcl.StderrLines)Check'CL stderr capture should work the same way'
nFail+←('logged'≡r.result)Check'the CL protocol stream must stay clean too'
JsonRpcCl.Disconnect hcl

⍝ --- 5. JSON-RPC error code/data survive an Mcp-layer signal --------
⍝ Mcp.ListTools/CallTool used to signal with resp.error.message alone,
⍝ dropping `code` (and `data`) entirely. ⎕SIGNAL can't carry a
⍝ structured payload of its own — it can only override names ⎕DMX
⍝ already defines — so the code goes into the message text for a human
⍝ and the whole error object onto h.LastError for a caller that needs
⍝ to branch on it. Verified against the real fff-mcp, whose
⍝ missing-required-argument path is a genuine ¯32602 invalid-params
⍝ error rather than a fixture's imitation of one.
exe←'C:\Users\stf\AppData\Local\fff-mcp\bin\fff-mcp.exe'
h←(WorkingDir:'D:\devel\mcp-client')Mcp.Connect,⊂exe
nFail+←(⍬≡h.LastError)Check'LastError should start empty'
:Trap 999
    {}h Mcp.CallTool'find_files' ⍝ no query given: invalid params
    nFail+←0 Check'expected a signal for missing required arguments'
:Else
    ⎕←'CallTool error signalled: ',⎕DMX.EM
    nFail+←(∨/'code ¯32602'⍷⎕DMX.EM)Check'the signalled message should name the JSON-RPC code'
:EndTrap
⎕←'LastError.code=',⍕h.LastError.code
nFail+←(¯32602≡h.LastError.code)Check'LastError should carry the structured error code'
nFail+←(0≠≢h.LastError.message)Check'LastError should carry the message too'
Mcp.Disconnect h

⍝ --- 6. Multiple concurrent child processes in one interpreter ------
⍝ Each Start/Connect takes its own ⎕TALLOC token range, so this was
⍝ designed to work but had never actually been run: three NDJSON
⍝ children and one Content-Length child, all alive at once, with
⍝ requests deliberately interleaved so a reply landing on the wrong
⍝ handle's queue (a shared-token bug) would show up as a wrong answer
⍝ rather than passing by luck.
hs←{JsonRpc.Connect toy}¨⍳3
names←'alpha' 'beta' 'gamma'
hcl←JsonRpcCl.Connect toycl
⍝ Fire every request before collecting any response — all four
⍝ processes are then mid-flight simultaneously.
ids←hs{⍺ JsonRpc.Send('echo'(text:⍵))}¨names
idcl←hcl JsonRpcCl.Send('echo'(text:'delta'))
got←hs{⍺ JsonRpc.AwaitResponse ⍵}¨ids
got←got.result
rcl←hcl JsonRpcCl.AwaitResponse idcl
⎕←'concurrent echoes: ',⍕got
⎕←'concurrent CL echo: ',rcl.result
nFail+←(got≡names)Check'each concurrent handle must get back its OWN answer, in order'
nFail+←('delta'≡rcl.result)Check'the CL handle must not be disturbed by the NDJSON ones'
⍝ Token ranges must be genuinely distinct, not merely unequal by luck.
toks←hs.Shell.Tok,hcl.Tok
⎕←'token bases: ',⍕toks
nFail+←((≢toks)=≢∪toks)Check'every concurrent handle needs its own token range'
⍝ Sums differ per handle so a crossed reply would be visible here too.
sums←hs{r←⍺ JsonRpc.Call('add'(a:⍵ ⋄ b:100)) ⋄ r.result}¨1 2 3
⎕←'concurrent adds: ',⍕sums
nFail+←(sums≡101 102 103)Check'concurrent adds must not cross handles'
{}JsonRpc.Disconnect¨hs
JsonRpcCl.Disconnect hcl
nFail+←(∧/'Exited'∘≡¨hs.Shell.Status)Check'every concurrent child should stop cleanly'
nFail+←(0=+/hs.Shell.Killed)Check'well-behaved concurrent children need no force-kill'

⎕←'nFail=',⍕nFail
:If nFail≠0
    ⎕←'FAIL: ',(⍕nFail),' check(s) failed'
:Else
    ⎕←'all checks passed'
:EndIf
⎕OFF
